            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "PROBRAHN"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Yummiest. Salad. Ever. I have made it several times now since last summer. I do love it with the shredded mozz, but I think cubed cheese (I like swiss) doesn't get mushy as easily. Truly delicious - the name doesn't do it justice. Even my 19-month-old gobbled it up (except she left the onions behind ;-) The thyme/olive oil/lemon juice combo is just phenomenal!"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "mbsebs"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Admittedly I took liberties with the basic recipe after reading the reviews and turned into a Greek salad. Used Feta instead of Mozzarella, oregano instead of thyme and added Greek olives! Made for a fantastic lunch!",
            "datePublished": "2020-09-28T19:02:23.417Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "yellowjaye"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I made this for a lunch today. I liked it and would make it again! I added capers and they were great, but I would not use the green olives again. I left out the palm, substituted lemon thyme for regular thyme, and used canned tomatoes in place of fresh ones. This was a great Mediterranean salad--thumbs up!",
            "datePublished": "2016-05-14T19:18:20.990Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Will Turnipseed"
            },
            "reviewBody": "10/10 would recommend. I added a can of olives and instead of cutting up a tomato, I bought grape tomatoes and cut those up. Oh I also added spring mix greens to it as well to give it more of a fresh flavor than a bunch of canned items. Lots of changes but isn't that what a salad is all about",
            "datePublished": "2019-02-21T16:20:08.470Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "J Flo'"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Great salad, I used the juice from 1/2 lemon which was more like 2 TBSP, organic canned tri-bean blend, and dried thyme. I added fresh cilantro which put this over the top - my picky daughter ate it!",
            "datePublished": "2013-02-03T11:47:17.193Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "jak"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I loved this salad and so did my guests. Super easy and fast. I’ll try adding capers… good idea!",
            "datePublished": "2025-01-02T06:24:32.377Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Sarah Jo"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I left out the hearts of palm because I know my family wouldn't eat it. I did use organic garbanzo beans(they just taste better) and stirred in about a 1/4 c. or so of greek yogurt. I liked this as did my older son. My husband was indifferent. My youngest wouldn't touch it. I think I might keep the basic ingredients of this recipe and perhaps mix this salad with some of 5thsister's greek yogurt dip. NOTE: I cannot stress enough to use fresh spices when you can and organic produce. It does make all the difference.",
            "datePublished": "2009-07-27T22:29:27.057Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Deni Davis"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This was great! The only change I made was using cannellini beans instead of garbanzo and apple cider vinegar instead of lemon juice. Other than that I followed the recipe exactly and loved it! Will definitely make this again!",
            "datePublished": "2012-07-28T11:13:55.330Z"
          },
          {
